  "body": "Add an optional MCP 2025-06-18 Streamable HTTP transport to CamCraft's external MCP client (`crates/app/src/mcp/`) for local servers that expose an HTTP endpoint instead of stdio.\n\n## Scope\n- Support MCP Streamable HTTP (`POST`/`GET` JSON-RPC over HTTP) behind `#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]`.\n- Reuse `crates/app/src/ai/endpoint.rs` (`Endpoint::parse`, `admit`, `admit_addrs`) and `reqwest` with no redirects and no proxy so plain `http://` and `offline_only` reach loopback hosts only.\n- Read optional server auth tokens from the OS keychain (`crates/app/src/ai/keychain.rs`) or environment variables. Never store tokens in `prefs.json` or `.camproj`, and never include tokens in error messages.\n- Enforce the same per-server trust, tool namespacing, per-call approval, and cloud privacy gates as the stdio transport.\n\nDone means: Fake loopback HTTP tests verify MCP `initialize`, `tools/list`, and `tools/call` over Streamable HTTP, refuse non-loopback `http://` and HTTP redirects before connecting, and confirm `prefs.json` stores zero tokens.\n\nPart of #3793\n",
